 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the New York state medical care facilities finance agency act,\nin relation to the ability to issue certain bonds and notes",
    "basePrintNo": "S6312",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6312-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7, NYS Med Care Fac Fin Ag Act",
    "lawSection": "New York State Medical Care Facilities Finance Agency Act",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6312\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the New York state medical care facilities finance agen-\ncy act, in relation to the ability to issue certain bonds and notes\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill would increase the authorization of the Dormitory Authority of\nthe State of New York (\"DASNY\"), as successor to the New York State\nMedical Care Facilities Finance Agency (\"MCFFA\") pursuant to the Health\nCare Financing Consolidation Act of 1995, to issue hospital and nursing\nhome project bonds and notes from $16.6 billion to $17.4 billion.\n\n \nSUMMERY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill would amend the MCFFA Act to increase DASNY's\nauthorization to issue hospital and nursing home project bonds and notes\nfrom $16.6 billion to $17.4 billion.\n\nSection two of the bill would make it effective immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, DASNY is authorized to issue to issue hospital and\nnursing home project bonds and notes in the amount of $16.6 billion.\nDASNY issues bonds for purposes including funding mortgage liens or\nproject loans to not-for-profit hospital and nursing home corporations.\nSome of the bonds issued for DASNY's hospital and nursing home clients\nare issued under the MCFFA Act. Bonds issued pursuant to the MCFFA Act\narc subject to the current hospital and nursing home project bond\nauthorization cap in the MCFFA Act of $16.6 billion. This authorization\nwas most recently increased by $800,000,000 in 2018. It was also\nincreased by $800,000,000 in 2009 and 2011.\n\nAs of January 30, 2020, DASNY has sold and closed bond transactions\npursuant to this authorization in the amount of $15,874,787,602.\nApproximately $560 million of capacity under the existing statutory\nlimitation is available for other transactions. Over the past few years\nDASNY has seen increased activity in the bond market, in terms of the\nnumber and size of the transactions. This 'bill is necessary to ensure\nthat DASNY has sufficient capacity to support additional healthcare\nprojects as they seek financing.\n\nAlthough DASNY cannot predict the timing- of future financings, DASNY\nis. seeking additional bond cap authorization now to ensure it may\nadequately respond to any future needs of its private not-for-profit\nhealth-care clients on a timely basis.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill. In 2009, the MCFFA bond cap was increased from $14.2\nbillion to $15 billion (Chapter 238 of the laws of 2009). The MCFFA bond\ncap was increased from $15 billion to $15.8 billion in 2011 (Chapter 516\nof the laws of 2011). In 2018, the MCFFA bond cap was increased from\n$15.8 billion to $16.6 billion (Chapter 183 of the laws of 2018).\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThe bill has no implications for the state budget.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n",
